# LEAVE THIS UNSET IN PRODUCTION. It should be empty on Vercel.
#
# vercel.json rewrites /api/* and /uploads/* through to the Render service,
# so the browser only ever talks to one origin and the client falls back to
# the relative "/api/v1" below. That is not a tidiness preference — it is
# what makes the session and gate cookies FIRST-PARTY. Point this at
# https://<api-host>/api/v1 instead and every cookie becomes a third-party
# cookie, which Safari and Brave drop outright and Chrome drops in Incognito
# or with tracking protection on. Sign-in then fails with "Invalid email or
# password" no matter how correct the password is, because the cookie the
# server set never comes back.
#
# Set it only when the API is genuinely on the same site (an api.<domain>
# subdomain of the site's own domain), or for a local build pointed at a
# remote API.
#
# VITE_API_URL=https://your-api-domain.com/api/v1
